nt, which an administrator creates for you."],[139,"Start New Project"],[749,"Start New Project"],[79,"Status"],[163,"Status"],[773,"Status"],[101,"Statuses"],[414,"Step"],[397,"Step 1 — Name the project"],[402,"Step 13 — Activate"],[398,"Step 2 — Build the region structure"],[400,"Step 9 — Add the staff"],[401,"Steps 10 to 12 — Routing, time limits and statuses"],[399,"Steps 3 to 8 — Define the vocabulary"],[217,"Subira inyuma"],[827,"Subira inyuma"],[228,"Submit"],[838,"Submit"],[439,"Submit a test complaint through the public website and confirm it appears\nfor the officer who should receive it."],[131,"Supervision"],[741,"Supervision"],[145,"System"],[755,"System"],[351,"Tab"],[100,"Tabs on a complaint"],[602,"Taking complaints from the public and entering them"],[138,"Tangiriza Umushinga Mushya"],[748,"Tangiriza Umushinga Mushya"],[335,"Tap **Back to Citizen Input Home** to record the next one."],[299,"Tap **Collect Reports from Citizens** on the home screen. What follows is a\nsix-step conversation. Each step shows you, in grey, the words to say to the\nperson in front of you — you can read them aloud as they are written."],[349,"Tap **Search Reports** on the home screen. It opens **Summary of Your Work**."],[388,"Tap **Sync Files** to see where things stand."],[370,"Tap **View Reports** on the home screen."],[361,"Tap any row."],[485,"Tell them they can check it at **egrm.risa.gov.rw/grm-portal** under\n**Track**, and that it will show the status but not their description."],[334,"Tell them they can check it at **egrm.risa.gov.rw/grm-portal** under\n**Track**, or by coming back to you with the code."],[22,"The **Mobile App** link is for field officers who collect complaints in places\nwith no internet. As a member of the public you do not need it — the website\ndoes everything you need."],[366,"The actions run in order, and only the next one is available. A complaint\nthat has just arrived offers **Accept Issue** and nothing else; once accepted\nit offers **Record Steps Taken**, then **Record Resolution**, then\n**Rate & Appeal**. **Escalate** sends it up to a supervisor when it cannot be\nsettled at your level."],[268,"The app is for **staff**, not for the public. Members of the public report\nproblems on the website at\n**egrm.risa.gov.rw/grm-portal** — see\nFor the public. You need a staff account to get past the\nsign-in screen."],[387,"The app keeps a copy of your work on the phone. You can record complaints all\nday with no network and lose nothing."],[276,"The app needs a working internet connection **the first time you sign in**,\nand again whenever you want to send in what you have collected. It does not\nneed one in between — see Working without signal."],[332,"The app produces a tracking code like `RDAP-260926-4369`."],[330,"The app shows everything you entered on one screen. Read the description back\nto the person and check the date. Anything wrong — go back with the arrow at\nthe top-left and fix it."],[258,"The assigned officer investigates, records what was done, and closes it. The\nstatus visible to the public updates at the same time."],[369,"The button is absent when no number was given, and when the person asked for\ntheir name to be kept confidential — in that case the screen shows\n**Confidential** and withholds the contact details along with the name."],[423,"The channels complaints arrive through"],[492,"The coloured pill in the **Imimerere** (*Status*) column shows where each one\nhas got to:"],[540,"The complaint itself — dates, category, description, region, status"],[343,"The complaints assigned to you"],[283,"The complaints assigned to you, grouped by stage"],[342,"The complaints assigned to you, the figures for your area, and how syncing works when you have no signal."],[346,"The figures for your area"],[273,"The first screen asks whether you have used the app before, and lets you pick\nyour language."],[34,"The form has four steps. A row of dots at the top shows how far along you are,\nand **Back** always returns to the previous step without losing what you typed."],[266,"The home screen"],[417,"The kinds of staff account the project has"],[532,"The list shows the tracking code, the status pill, and the reference. The grey\nboxes along the top filter it — by project, category, department, assignee,\nissue type, status or region. Newly arrived complaints carry the\n**Gishya** (*New*) pill."],[574,"The main screen"],[261,"The mobile app"],[312,"The name is **optional**. Say so out loud — the screen tells you to. If they\nwould rather not be named, leave it blank and move on; the complaint is\nrecorded exactly the same way."],[360,"The newest is at the top — so a complaint you have just recorded appears\nfirst, with **0 days ago** against it."],[86,"The officer has recorded an outcome."],[462,"The project this belongs to"],[260,"The public website screenshots in this guide show the **English** version, so\nthey match the English text around them. The staff screens are shown in\n**Kinyarwanda**, because that is what staff accounts on this system actually\ndisplay. Every staff label is also listed in English on the\nScreen labels page."],[486,"The quality of a complaint depends almost entirely on what you capture at this\nmoment. Before you save, check you have:"],[336,"The quality of a complaint is decided entirely in this conversation. Before\nStep 5, check you have:"],[329,"The region decides **who receives the complaint**. If the place the person\ndescribes is not in a region you cover, record it anyway, name the exact\nplace in the description, and tell your administrator afterwards."],[290,"The six-step Citizen Input flow — what to ask at each step, and what to hand back at the end."],[598,"The staff screens display in **Kinyarwanda**, because that is the language\nthis system is set to. The Screen labels page lists every\nlabel you will meet with its English meaning. If you would rather work in\nEnglish, ask your administrator to set the language on your own account — it\nchanges only what you see, not what anyone else sees."],[256,"The system gives the complaint a code like `RDAP-260907-6503`. Anyone holding\nthat code can check the status without logging in."],[259,"The system opens in **Kinyarwanda**. The public website also offers\n**English** and **Français**, and you can switch at any time using the\nselector in the top-right corner."],[534,"The tabs across the top separate the record into sections:"],[407,"The title, an optional start and end date, and the locale — country, default\nlanguage, number and date format, time zone."],[91,"The tracking page deliberately shows only the status, category and submission\ndate. It does not show your description, your contact details, or the names of\nthe officers involved. This is so that a tracking code shared with or\noverheard by someone else cannot expose personal information."],[3,"The two things you can do"],[419,"The units that complaints can be assigned to"],[16,"The website opens in Kinyarwanda. To read it in another language, use the\nselector at the **top-right** of any page. Three choices are available:"],[427,"The wording of the messages the system sends"],[411,"Then load the actual regions into those levels. They can be imported rather\nthan typed one by one."],[482,"Then save."],[65,"Then see Check a complaint."],[331,"Then tap **SUBMIT**."],[386,"These are the figures used to decide which channels the public actually rely\non, which is why getting the channel right at\nStep 3 matters."],[413,"These steps set the lists people will choose from. Each is a simple table you\nadd rows to."],[310,"They want an SMS or email, and will give you the number or address"],[306,"They want nothing sent to them at all"],[308,"They will come back to you for news — the safest default"],[248,"This guide assumes no technical background. Pick the description below that\nsounds like you."],[77,"This is the code you were given when you submitted, in the form\n`RDAP-26090